  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 128 AM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nModels show the upper high shifting back to the west with the upper \nridge over the region through the weekend into next week. This will \ncontinue the hot, humid, and dry weather into next week. Highs are \nexpected to remain in the upper 90s to low 100s into the middle of \nnext week with triple digit heat indices across the area and values \nof 105F to 110F across portions of the fa each day. Heat headlines \nwill also likely persist across at least portions of the fa into \nnext week.\n\nThe moisture is forecast to remain in the area which will keep fire \nweather conditions from becoming elevated. However, as previously \nmentioned, the very dry fuels will remain susceptible to wildfires \nand will likely continue to do so until the area receives some much \nneeded rainfall. With that in mind, everyone needs to continue to be \ncautious and take steps to prevent fire starts.",
